course: dictionary
lesson: 573
title: Australian: from a place, or a person
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word Australian tells you where something comes from or belongs. Used before a noun, it is an adjective: in «the Australian frilled lizard», Australian tells you which lizard, the one from Australia. Look at the word after it to see what it describes.
explain: Used alone, Australian names a person, so it is a noun. «Most Australians live near the coasts, where it rains more.» The -s means more than one person. Australian always starts with a capital letter, because it names a country.
explain: Context gives the clue. In «Australian animals», the word animals tells you Australian means belonging to Australia. Test it by swapping in your meaning: «animals from Australia» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Australian means from or belonging to Australia, or its people or language.
fact: An Australian is a person from Australia. An Aussie is an informal word for an Australian.
fact: Australia is a country and a continent in the Southern Hemisphere, and its capital is Canberra.
fact: Many Australian animals, such as kangaroos and koalas, are marsupials that are found nowhere else in the world.
fact: Australian seasons are the opposite of those in the UK, so Christmas is in summer. Australian English has words like «arvo», which means afternoon.
exercise: «The Australian frilled lizard opens a huge neck frill to scare predators.» What does Australian describe here? | The neck frill | The predators | *The lizard, which comes from Australia | The hissing
exercise: «Most Australians live near the coasts.» What is an Australian? | A place near the sea | *A person from Australia | An animal that hisses | A kind of shoe
exercise: «Australian English has words like arvo and brekkie.» Find and copy the word that tells you where the English comes from. | English | words | arvo | *Australian
test: What does Australian mean in the phrase «the Australian outback»? | *From or belonging to Australia | A kind of lizard | Very hot and dry | Far away from the sea
test: Which word is Australian English for flip-flops? | Brekkie | *Thongs | Arvo | Mate
exam: Which sentence uses Australians as a noun, meaning people? | «The Australian frilled lizard hisses at predators.» | «Australian English has words like arvo.» | *«Most Australians live near the coasts, where it rains more.» | «Christmas is in summer for Australian families.»
